  "AuthFlow": "oauth2-cc",
  "AuthFlowNote": "OAuth 2.0 Client Credentials grant (RFC 6749 §4.4). The service application uses client_id + client_secret (or client_assertion for certificate-based) to obtain a Bearer token from the tenant-specific token endpoint without user interaction. No refresh_token is issued for client_credentials — re-acquire by submitting a new token request when the current token is within expiry. Source: Microsoft Entra v2-oauth2-client-creds-grant-flow docs.",
  "AuthHeaderPattern": "Authorization: Bearer <access_token>",
  "AuthHeaderPatternSource": "Microsoft Graph auth-concepts page: the app attaches the access token as a Bearer token to the Authorization header. Example: Authorization: Bearer <token_value>. Source: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/graph/auth/auth-concepts",
  "TokenEndpointPattern": "https://login.microsoftonline.com/{tenant}/oauth2/v2.0/token",
  "TokenEndpointNote": "tenant is the Azure AD tenant ID (GUID) or domain name — NEVER a constant baked into the connector. Mechanism: POST with Content-Type application/x-www-form-urlencoded body: client_id={clientId}&client_secret={clientSecret}&grant_type=client_credentials&scope=https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2F.default. The /.default scope requests all application permissions pre-consented for the app registration. Source: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity-platform/v2-oauth2-client-creds-grant-flow",
  "TokenScopeRequired": "https://graph.microsoft.com/.default",
